other like you're ...

263
00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:26.199
No. It's chaos. madness.

264
00:14:26.282 --> 00:14:27.742
You don't trust me
with your best friend ?

265
00:14:27.826 --> 00:14:29.911
You don't trust me
with your baby brother ?

266
00:14:30.829 --> 00:14:33.331
Okay. Okay. I'll
stay for a while.

267
00:14:34.541 --> 00:14:35.583
But there will be
no more flirting.

268
00:14:36.668 --> 00:14:37.669
Literally none.

269
00:14:37.669 --> 00:14:38.920
So. Dr. Korby.

270
00:14:39.045 --> 00:14:40.922
Uh. Sam. I got to
say. I'm a big fan

271
00:14:41.006 --> 00:14:42.966
of your work on advanced
ancient cultures.

272
00:14:43.091 --> 00:14:46.302
-I read that your latest dig was on Vadia Nine.
-Uh-huh.

273
00:14:46.428 --> 00:14:48.263
Uh. have you
climbed Mount Caleb ?

274
00:14:48.346 --> 00:14:49.806
Uh. we did. actually. Yeah.

275
00:14:49.931 --> 00:14:52.600
It was. it was
pretty romantic. actually.

276
00:14:52.684 --> 00:14:54.185
Uh. Mr. Spock.

277
00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:56.479
Glad you could join us.

278
00:14:57.856 --> 00:14:59.399
I finished my work early.

279
00:14:59.399 --> 00:15:02.777
Dr. Korby was just about to
tell us a romantic story.

280
00:15:02.861 --> 00:15:04.404
-Oh. no. don't worry about it.
-No.

281
00:15:04.404 --> 00:15:05.780
-Some other time.
-You guys don't want to hear ...

282
00:15:05.864 --> 00:15:06.948
-Bore the life out of you.
-Yeah.

283
00:15:07.032 --> 00:15:08.366
I would
like to hear it.

284
00:15:08.491 --> 00:15:10.535
I have. of late. become
a student of romance.

285
00:15:11.828 --> 00:15:15.498
Sudden thirst. Beto. give
me a hand with some drinks.

286
00:15:16.499 --> 00:15:19.377
Okay. Um ... Well.

287
00:15:19.377 --> 00:15:21.296
uh. when I was a little girl.

288
00:15:21.379 --> 00:15:22.922
whenever I would go
away on a trip ...

289
00:15:23.006 --> 00:15:25.133
to camp. to school ...

290
00:15:25.216 --> 00:15:27.844
my mother would
always say to me.

291
00:15:27.927 --> 00:15:30.096
"Chrissy. I hope
you find the sun ..."

292
00:15:30.096 --> 00:15:34.184
"I hope you find the sun
and the moon and the stars."

293
00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:36.186
Yeah.

294
00:15:36.311 --> 00:15:39.397
And they turned out
to be the last words

295
00:15:39.397 --> 00:15:41.483
she ever said to me.

296
00:15:41.566 --> 00:15:43.026
And. um.

297
00:15:43.109 --> 00:15:45.278
Mount Caleb actually happens
to break the solar plane.

298
00:15:45.278 --> 00:15:48.198
So. um. the sun and the moon
are visible at the same time.

299
00:15:48.281 --> 00:15:50.241
And it was my mother's birthday.

300
00:15:50.367 --> 00:15:53.203
And I didn't tell anybody
'cause I never do.

301
00:15:53.328 --> 00:15:58.416
Uh. but he just noticed
that I was down and ...

302
00:15:58.541 --> 00:16:02.671
remembered the story and
put two and two together.

303
00:16:02.754 --> 00:16:05.632
And when we got to the top ...

304
00:16:05.632 --> 00:16:07.050
When we got to the top.

305
00:16:07.133 --> 00:16:10.720
I showed her the stunning sky

306
00:16:10.804 --> 00:16:14.015
and gave her this.

307
00:16:15.433 --> 00:16:17.394
Tilaryan Star Gems.

308
00:16:17.519 --> 00:16:19.771
-They're incredibly rare.
-Yeah.

309
00:16:19.896 --> 00:16:22.273
And he said.

310
00:16:22.399 --> 00:16:24.609
"You looked sad.

311
00:16:24.609 --> 00:16:28.655
I wanted to give you the sun
and the moon and the stars."

312
00:16:40.792 --> 00:16:42.335
-Libations.
-Shots. everybody !

313
00:16:42.419 --> 00:16:44.879
-Fun.
-Thank God.

314
00:16:46.256 --> 00:16:48.133
Ooh. that's a cool bracelet.
Where'd you get it ?

315
00:17:05.817 --> 00:17:07.694
Good evening.

316
00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:10.572
Ready for a change ?

317
00:17:10.655 --> 00:17:12.782
I was not aware we had
a Vulcan bartender.

318
00:17:12.866 --> 00:17:14.743
Temporary posting.

319
00:17:14.826 --> 00:17:16.286
Just passing through.

320
00:17:16.411 --> 00:17:20.331
So. something
different but better ?

321
00:17:20.331 --> 00:17:22.459
Something you definitely want ?

322
00:17:22.584 --> 00:17:24.961
Yes. that would be fine.

323
00:17:25.086 --> 00:17:26.963
Fantastic.

324
00:17:27.088 --> 00:17:30.800
I have just the thing.

325
00:17:31.593 --> 00:17:34.304
Swirl it around.
Brings out the aroma.

326
00:17:35.805 --> 00:17:36.765
Don't drink it too fast.

327
00:17:36.848 --> 00:17:38.975
It'll go right to your head.

328
00:17:42.645 --> 00:17:43.605
Hmm.

329
00:18:19.391 --> 00:18:21.226
Good morning.

330
00:18:27.148 --> 00:18:29.651
Good morning back.

331
00:18:33.029 --> 00:18:35.573
Tonight. no sleepover.

332
00:18:36.366 --> 00:18:40.161
It is bad luck to see your bride
on the day of your wedding.

333
00:18:50.005 --> 00:18:51.089
Science
Officer's personal log.

334
00:18:51.089 --> 00:18:53.174
Stardate 2251.7.

335
00:18:53.258 --> 00:18:54.759
After a three-month billet.

336
00:18:54.884 --> 00:18:56.845
the battle scars of our
encounter with the Gorn

337
00:18:56.970 --> 00:18:58.555
are all but erased.

338
00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:00.390
And while docked
at Starbase One.

339
00:19:00.515 --> 00:19:03.977
our crew prepares to celebrate
a rare and joyous occasion.

340
00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:07.897
the wedding nuptials between
myself and Nurse Chapel.

341
00:19:07.981 --> 00:19:09.607
Your first dance
is going to be great.

342
00:19:09.607 --> 00:19:10.817
You're improving.

343
00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:12.068
Untrue.

344
00:19:15.363 --> 00:19:16.781
I've never understood
the need for deception

345
00:19:16.865 --> 00:19:19.701
to smooth a potential
negative reaction.

346
00:19:19.784 --> 00:19:23.204
You're just going
to excel at marriage.

347
00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:25.665
Have you ever been married ?

348
00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:27.751
Me ? God no.

349
00:19:27.751 --> 00:19:29.919
I'm not really the
commitment type.

350
00:19:31.087 --> 00:19:34.924
My childhood didn't really set
me up for a stable attachment.

351
00:19:35.717 --> 00:19:38.845
Now. shooting backwards
while running.

352
00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:40.805
that I can do.

353
00:19:41.639 --> 00:19:45.101
Of late. I must say you
have seemed lighter.

354
00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:49.731
Spock. if you don't
have it by now.

355
00:19:49.814 --> 00:19:51.441
then it's too late.

356
00:19:51.524 --> 00:19:53.026
Thank you. La'An.

357
00:19:53.109 --> 00:19:54.611
You have been a
good friend to me.

358
00:19:54.611 --> 00:19:57.113
I must prepare
for the rehearsal.

359
00:20:04.788 --> 00:20:07.832
Places. everyone !
We have much to do.

360
00:20:07.832 --> 00:20:10.210
A wedding doesn't just plan
itself overnight. you know.

361
00:20:10.335 --> 00:20:12.879
And the rehearsal is
just like the real thing.

362
00:20:12.962 --> 00:20:14.714
only with comfortable shoes.

363
00:20:14.839 --> 00:20:16.633
This wedding planner
of yours is something.

364
00:20:16.633 --> 00:20:20.679
Never thought of Andorians
as being so detail-oriented.

365
00:20:20.679 --> 00:20:22.263
Hmm.

366
00:20:22.389 --> 00:20:24.224
You two. you're
like two peas in a space pod.

367
00:20:24.307 --> 00:20:25.725
So delightful.

368
00:20:25.809 --> 00:20:28.395
-Let's start with the cake.
-Wait. uh. where's Roger ?

369
00:20:28.478 --> 00:20:31.064
I feel like we should
probably wait for my best man.

370
00:20:31.147 --> 00:20:32.148
I'm here.

371
00:20:32.148 --> 00:20:33.608
I am here.

372
00:20:33.692 --> 00:20:34.901
And I have the cakes.

373
00:20:34.984 --> 00:20:36.736
-Excellent.
-Oh. yeah. Very nice.

374
00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:38.947
Christine. I
couldn't just chat ...

375
00:20:39.072 --> 00:20:40.490
Uh. later. Mr. Korby.

376
00:20:40.573 --> 00:20:41.991
Doctor.

377
00:20:42.117 --> 00:20:44.327
-Dr. Korby.
-Fine.

378
00:20:44.452 --> 00:20:46.413
Actually. I have a
special best man task

379
00:20:46.496 --> 00:20:47.706
just for you.

380
00:20:47.706 --> 00:20:50.208
Could you wait for
me way over there ?

381
00:20:50.208 --> 00:20:52.210
Quick as you can.

382
00:20:54.754 --> 00:20:56.881
Good one. Now. Mr. Spock.

383
00:20:56.881 --> 00:20:59.592
I know you wanted to embrace
a human-type wedding.

384
00:20:59.676 --> 00:21:02.178
but what about fusion style ?

385
00:21:02.303 --> 00:21:05.015
I call this "Hu-can."

386
00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:07.809
Or "Vul-man."

387
00:21:07.892 --> 00:21:10.103
Just try it.

388
00:21:15.942 --> 00:21:17.068
You hate it ?

389
00:21:18.153 --> 00:21:23.158
I was not expecting cake with
quite so much heat and brine.

390
00:21:36.087 --> 00:21:38.465
Let's try that again. shall we ?

391
00:21:38.548 --> 00:21:39.883
Oh. I'll go.

392
00:21:42.135 --> 00:21:43.345
Spock's joking.
this is delicious.

393
00:21:43.428 --> 00:21:46.306
Is it chocolate and. um ...

394
00:21:46.431 --> 00:21:47.599
Vulcan pahklor ?

395
00:21:47.599 --> 00:21:49.309
Indeed. pahklor.

396
00:21:49.392 --> 00:21:52.437
Nothing says love like pahklor.

397
00:21:53.229 --> 00:21:54.689
I must've
been mistaken before.

398
00:21:54.814 --> 00:21:56.066
This is quite good.

399
00:21:56.191 --> 00:21:57.650
Not just good but perfect.

400
00:21:57.734 --> 00:21:59.778
like your wedding
is going to be.

401
00:22:01.654 --> 00:22:03.406
Let's talk about choreography.

402
00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:07.327
Spock. assuming we're not going
to have a Kal-if-ee situation.

403
00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:09.371
I have you over on the altar

404
00:22:09.454 --> 00:22:13.541
and your best man Captain
Pike in the front row

405
00:22:13.625 --> 00:22:14.793
just here.

406
00:22:14.793 --> 00:22:16.336
Joseph and Una.

407
00:22:16.419 --> 00:22:21.716
I see you waltzing
Christine down the aisle

408
00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:24.094
and then spin her
into Spock's arms.

409
00:22:24.219 --> 00:22:25.679
I didn't practice that.

410
00:22:25.762 --> 00:22:28.348
I have a surprise for
you. my blushing bride.

411
00:22:28.431 --> 00:22:31.601
Arrived all the way
from Vermont. Earth

412
00:22:31.726 --> 00:22:33.895
this morning.

413
00:22:33.978 --> 00:22:35.271
My mother's flowers ?

414
00:22:36.272 --> 00:22:38.942
She had these preserved
after her wedding.

415
00:22:48.952 --> 00:22:50.745
Oh. no.

416
00:22:50.829 --> 00:22:53.957
Those
flowers look dead.

417
00:22:53.957 --> 00:22:56.459
These were supposed to be
stored at exactly 2.7 degrees.

418
00:22:56.584 --> 00:22:58.586
-I mean. the ...
-I'm so sorry. Christine.

419
00:22:58.712 --> 00:23:00.130
Is there any way
to salvage them ?

420
00:23:00.255 --> 00:23:01.965
I-I have a rehydrator
in my quarters.

421
00:23:01.965 --> 00:23:03.258
I'll tell you what.

422
00:23:03.341 --> 00:23:05.927
Maybe they just need to breathe.

423
00:23:19.649 --> 00:23:21.067
I mean ...

424
00:23:22.861 --> 00:23:25.071
Oh. my God.
What ?

425
00:23:25.155 --> 00:23:27.198
It worked. I can't believe it.

426
00:23:28.533 --> 00:23:29.784
This is why we have rehearsal.

427
00:23:29.909 --> 00:23:32.287
And with that avertation
of the latest crisis.

428
00:23:32.412 --> 00:23:33.413
let's continue.

429
00:23:33.496 --> 00:23:34.789
With both at the altar.

430
00:23:34.873 --> 00:23:38.418
we have the rings
exchanged. and voilà.

431
00:23:38.418 --> 00:23:40.462
Everyone's as happy
as a Ternaran bat.

432
00:23:40.545 --> 00:23:43.131
Uh. Christine. can we just
chat for two seconds. please ?

433
00:23:43.214 --> 00:23:45.633
Unfortunately. rehearsal
has just finished.

434
00:23:45.717 --> 00:23:48.887
which means. Nurse Chapel. I'm
gonna have to scoop you away

435
00:23:49.012 --> 00:23:50.430
for your final fitting.

436
00:23:50.430 --> 00:23:52.557
So quickly. here we go.

437
00:23:52.682 --> 00:23:54.517
Please tell me you're not gonna
wear that jacket on the day.

438
00:23:54.601 --> 00:23:55.935
Korbs.

439
00:24:04.903 --> 00:24:06.905
Hey. how are you ?
How're you doing ?

440
00:24:38.478 --> 00:24:42.148
Dr. Korby. what are you doing ?

441
00:24:43.858 --> 00:24:45.402
I'm. um ...

442
00:24:46.569 --> 00:24:48.113
 ...trying to delete your vows.

443
00:24:48.113 --> 00:24:50.323
I knew it. The
cake. the flowers.

444
00:24:50.323 --> 00:24:51.991
you are trying to
sabotage our wedding.

445
00:24:51.991 --> 00:24:54.494
Yeah. y-you can't
marry Christine.

446
00:24:54.577 --> 00:24:55.954
Are you in love with her ?

447
00:24:56.079 --> 00:24:58.623
Yes. But that's not the reason.

448
00:24:58.623 --> 00:25:00.041
Well. not entirely.

449
00:25:00.125 --> 00:25:03.420
Look. this wedding is not
supposed to happen. okay ?

450
00:25:03.545 --> 00:25:05.380
Uh. I can't fully explain it.

451
00:25:05.505 --> 00:25:07.549
but our reality has shifted.

452
00:25:07.632 --> 00:25:09.509
-I think you should leave. Doctor.
-Just listen.

453
00:25:09.592 --> 00:25:11.469
Yesterday. Christine and I
arrived on the Enterprise

454
00:25:11.553 --> 00:25:13.096
to attend the
Federation's Centennial.

455
00:25:13.179 --> 00:25:15.306
We specifically chose the
centennial as our wedding day.

456
00:25:15.306 --> 00:25:17.559
No. no. no. no. It is
the reason we are here.

457
00:25:17.642 --> 00:25:20.603
As of yesterday.
there was no wedding.

458
00:25:20.687 --> 00:25:23.273
There was no "you
and Nurse Chapel."

459
00:25:23.398 --> 00:25:24.858
She and I were together.

460
00:25:24.858 --> 00:25:27.110
You arrived together because
you are best friends.

461
00:25:27.235 --> 00:25:30.739
No. not as best friends.
romantically we are together.

462
00:25:30.864 --> 00:25:34.367
But I seem to be the only
one here that remembers that.

463
00:25:34.367 --> 00:25:36.494
I proposed to Christine
three months ago.

464
00:25:36.619 --> 00:25:38.329
before she embarked on
her fellowship with you.

465
00:25:38.329 --> 00:25:40.081
I procured my grandmother's
engagement ring ...

466
00:25:40.165 --> 00:25:41.416
None of that happened.

467
00:25:41.541 --> 00:25:43.585
Why am I the only one
that remembers this ?

468
00:25:43.668 --> 00:25:45.503
You parted ways
before the fellowship.

469
00:25:45.503 --> 00:25:47.756
And yeah. when I met her. at
first. she was pretty gloomy.

470
00:25:47.839 --> 00:25:49.758
I get it. endings
are ... are difficult.

471
00:25:49.841 --> 00:25:51.259
I think you should
visit sickbay. Doc ...

472
00:25:51.343 --> 00:25:52.469
Wait.

473
00:25:52.552 --> 00:25:55.972
At first. she was a fellow. yes.

474
00:25:56.097 --> 00:25:58.850
But she quickly became more.

475
00:25:58.850 --> 00:26:00.393
An equal.

476
00:26:01.144 --> 00:26:03.063
After a while. she was
running the excavation site

477
00:26:03.146 --> 00:26:05.148
on Vadia Nine with me.

478
00:26:05.231 --> 00:26:08.109
And one night. we stayed late.

479
00:26:08.860 --> 00:26:12.530
And I read her a poem by Neruda.

480
00:26:14.449 --> 00:26:20.121
"I crave your mouth.
your voice. your hair."

481
00:26:21.706 --> 00:26:23.416
And she. um ...

482
00:26:24.209 --> 00:26:25.502
She kissed me ...

483
00:26:37.097 --> 00:26:39.057
Oh. no.

484
00:26:41.142 --> 00:26:42.811
Oh. no.

485
00:26:50.902 --> 00:26:53.154
Please. Dr. Korby.

486
00:26:53.238 --> 00:26:54.698
I owe you an apology.

487
00:26:54.823 --> 00:26:57.951
Yes. for that. But
also. you were right.

488
00:26:57.951 --> 00:26:59.244
Reality has been changed.

489
00:26:59.244 --> 00:27:01.246
None of this is
how it should be.

490
00:27:01.246 --> 00:27:02.914
-So you remember ?
-I do.

491
00:27:03.039 --> 00:27:04.749
But I am not entirely sure why.

492
00:27:04.749 --> 00:27:06.251
Have you tried
telling Christine ?

493
00:27:06.251 --> 00:27:07.711
Yes. but she shut me down.

494
00:27:07.836 --> 00:27:09.462
I've considered several
possible explanations

495
00:27:09.462 --> 00:27:11.006
for this mass delusion.

496
00:27:11.131 --> 00:27:12.966
First. that this is an
alternate dimension.

497
00:27:12.966 --> 00:27:15.719
I've already checked myself for
phase variance and found none.

498
00:27:15.844 --> 00:27:18.930
Exposure to an
environmental hallucinogen.

499
00:27:19.055 --> 00:27:21.057
Christine and I arrived
at the same time. so ...

500
00:27:21.141 --> 00:27:23.101
You would both be unaffected.

501
00:27:23.226 --> 00:27:24.519
Alien virus ?

502
00:27:24.602 --> 00:27:26.146
The bio-filters have
been recently upgraded.

503
00:27:26.229 --> 00:27:29.357
Perhaps an improbability field ?

504
00:27:29.441 --> 00:27:33.528
We once entered one
that made us ... sing.

505
00:27:33.653 --> 00:27:34.738
Perhaps.

506
00:27:34.863 --> 00:27:36.281
Now that I am aware
of the situation.

507
00:27:36.364 --> 00:27:39.701
I will obviously not
proceed with the nuptials.

508
00:27:42.287 --> 00:27:44.080
You may not have a choice.

509
00:27:45.290 --> 00:27:47.208
Every time I've tried
to stop this wedding.

510
00:27:47.334 --> 00:27:49.836
something has interfered.

511
00:27:49.919 --> 00:27:51.254
You are suggesting the presence

512
00:27:51.379 --> 00:27:52.630
of an advanced
intelligent life-form

513
00:27:52.630 --> 00:27:54.341
with reality-altering
capabilities.

514
00:27:54.341 --> 00:27:55.425
Yes.

515
00:27:55.508 --> 00:27:57.427
But why leave you unaffected ?

516
00:27:57.510 --> 00:27:58.678
Well ...

517
00:27:59.763 --> 00:28:01.723
 ...my rigorous
intellect may have

518
00:28:01.806 --> 00:28:04.267
shielded my mind
from the illusion.

519
00:28:05.977 --> 00:28:07.228
Doctor.

520
00:28:07.312 --> 00:28:09.272
If one of our intellects
could bestow immunity.

521
00:28:09.397 --> 00:28:11.775
I am confident it
would not be yours.

522
00:28:15.820 --> 00:28:18.365
Come. We can use the science
lab to scan the ship.

523
00:28:18.365 --> 00:28:21.201
Any anomalous energy
should be detectable.

524
00:28:22.660 --> 00:28:25.747
Great. Another
Andorian annoyance.

525
00:28:25.830 --> 00:28:27.123
Ah. there you are !

526
00:28:27.248 --> 00:28:29.292
Greetings and many felicitations

527
00:28:29.417 --> 00:28:31.670
on this happiest
of wedding eves.

528
00:28:31.795 --> 00:28:33.546
-Oh. Mr. Korby.
-Doctor.

529
00:28:33.630 --> 00:28:35.048
You really are
everywhere. aren't you ?

530
00:28:35.131 --> 00:28:36.466
Bit like a rash.

531
00:28:36.549 --> 00:28:38.635
Speaking of which. the
rest of the bridal party

532
00:28:38.760 --> 00:28:39.969
are enjoying facials.

533
00:28:40.095 --> 00:28:41.596
Perhaps you should join them.

534
00:28:41.680 --> 00:28:43.807
You do look a little
dull. Are you sleeping ?

535
00:28:43.932 --> 00:28:46.768
The bags beneath
your eyes say no.

536
00:28:46.851 --> 00:28:49.396
My darling groom. what
do you think of this ?

537
00:28:49.479 --> 00:28:51.272
The color really
brings out your eyes.

538
00:28:51.356 --> 00:28:53.066
Could this wait ? I have
urgent duties to attend to.

539
00:28:53.149 --> 00:28:54.567
Don't be silly.

540
00:28:54.567 --> 00:28:57.153
Right now. your most important
mission is matrimony.

541
00:28:59.989 --> 00:29:01.533
That one will be fine.

542
00:29:01.658 --> 00:29:03.159
Come. We must go.

543
00:29:03.284 --> 00:29:04.828
It's Doctor.

544
00:29:04.953 --> 00:29:06.996
"It's Doctor."

545
00:29:09.749 --> 00:29:11.001
Nice lab.

546
00:29:11.793 --> 00:29:14.963
Initiating ship-wide scan now.
It will take a few minutes.

547
00:29:15.046 --> 00:29:18.008
I was thinking about how it was
that you became disillusioned.

548
00:29:18.133 --> 00:29:19.509
At the moment I punched you.

549
00:29:19.592 --> 00:29:22.595
it was as if a fog
in my mind lifted.

550
00:29:22.679 --> 00:29:24.097
and I knew.

551
00:29:24.180 --> 00:29:26.099
Perhaps it was the sudden burst

552
00:29:26.099 --> 00:29:28.101
of adrenaline and
cortisol that did it.

553
00:29:28.101 --> 00:29:29.728
It is also possible
that whatever power

554
00:29:29.853 --> 00:29:31.646
is creating this false
reality cannot be maintained

555
00:29:31.730 --> 00:29:33.565
when so directly
confronted with the truth.

556
00:29:33.565 --> 00:29:35.483
Regardless. we must find a way

557
00:29:35.567 --> 00:29:37.360
to communicate the
situation to the captain.

558
00:29:37.444 --> 00:29:39.029
Good luck with that.

559
00:29:39.154 --> 00:29:40.405
There you are.

560
00:29:40.405 --> 00:29:42.323
You were supposed to
meet me in your quarters.

561
00:29:42.407 --> 00:29:43.825
Whatever this is. I cannot.

562
00:29:43.950 --> 00:29:45.827
Sam ! What do we have here ?

563
00:29:45.910 --> 00:29:49.372
These are the wine selections
for the head table tomorrow.

564
00:29:53.418 --> 00:29:57.047
Listen to me very
carefully. Lieutenant Kirk.

565
00:29:57.130 --> 00:29:58.965
Enterprise came to Starbase One

566
00:29:59.049 --> 00:30:01.384
to celebrate the
Federation Centennial.

567
00:30:01.509 --> 00:30:03.261
Not a wedding.

568
00:30:03.386 --> 00:30:05.722
Nurse Chapel and I are
no longer a couple.

569
00:30:05.847 --> 00:30:07.682
We are not getting married.

570
00:30:07.807 --> 00:30:10.727
You are suffering from
an unknown phenomenon.

571
00:30:10.852 --> 00:30:13.521
It is possible we
are all under attack.

572
00:30:15.023 --> 00:30:16.524
I get it.

573
00:30:17.442 --> 00:30:19.652
I get it. Spock.
you have cold feet.

574
00:30:19.736 --> 00:30:21.613
-It's totally normal. look ...
-Punch me.

575
00:30:21.738 --> 00:30:22.947
What ?

576
00:30:25.408 --> 00:30:27.202
I'm not gonna punch you.

577
00:30:27.327 --> 00:30:28.370
You are sloppy.

578
00:30:28.495 --> 00:30:30.622
Less intelligent
than your brother.

579
00:30:31.539 --> 00:30:32.999
No one likes your mustache.

580
00:30:37.712 --> 00:30:40.090
And you have terrible
taste in wine.

581
00:30:45.970 --> 00:30:48.014
If I gave you a black eye
the day before your wedding.

582
00:30:48.014 --> 00:30:49.432
Christine would kill me.

583
00:30:49.516 --> 00:30:51.017
Scan complete.

584
00:30:51.017 --> 00:30:53.895
There are no anomalous
energy readings present.

585
00:30:55.271 --> 00:30:56.940
Perhaps the chardonnay.

586
00:30:58.191 --> 00:31:00.402
Sir. we have an
urgent situation.

587
00:31:00.485 --> 00:31:02.237
I am aware. Lieutenant.

588
00:31:05.115 --> 00:31:07.826
And there. Fixed that.

589
00:31:07.826 --> 00:31:11.454
Mr. Spock. welcome to
your bachelor party.

590
00:31:11.538 --> 00:31:13.081
-Hey.
-Spock-o !

591
00:31:13.164 --> 00:31:14.290
Spock !

592
00:31:14.416 --> 00:31:15.417
I prepared all
of your favorites.

593
00:31:15.500 --> 00:31:17.335
Jumbo mollusk. Pok-tar.

594
00:31:17.460 --> 00:31:19.254
and look what I found.

595
00:31:19.337 --> 00:31:20.880
Lutrog.

596
00:31:20.880 --> 00:31:24.217
And something imbibable for
the rest of us: Saurian brandy.

597
00:31:24.217 --> 00:31:25.552
Hmm ?

598
00:31:25.635 --> 00:31:27.762
Oh. honestly. I'm not
really much of a drinker.

599
00:31:27.846 --> 00:31:29.347
I hardly touch the stuff.

600
00:31:29.347 --> 00:31:31.057
I believe tradition dictates

601
00:31:31.057 --> 00:31:33.601
the groom-to-be give us a toast
before he walks the plank.

602
00:31:33.685 --> 00:31:36.021
-Yes. speech.
-Speech.

603
00:31:36.021 --> 00:31:38.440
Come on. Mr. Spock.

604
00:31:39.983 --> 00:31:42.527
Our reality has been changed.

605
00:31:43.278 --> 00:31:45.113
Nurse Chapel and I
are not together.

606
00:31:45.196 --> 00:31:47.115
She is in love with Dr. Korby.

607
00:31:47.198 --> 00:31:49.451
and only he and I remember this.

608
00:31:53.705 --> 00:31:57.709
To Spock. the luckiest
man in the world.

609
00:31:57.834 --> 00:31:58.710
Yes. to Spock.

610
00:31:58.835 --> 00:32:00.337
-Mr. Spock.
-Cheers.

611
00:32:01.963 --> 00:32:05.050
Captain. Enterprise is
experiencing a mass delusion.

612
00:32:05.175 --> 00:32:06.384
I told you. Cold feet.

613
00:32:06.509 --> 00:32:07.761
My feet are perfectly
warm. thank you.

614
00:32:07.844 --> 00:32:10.055
This is serious.

615
00:32:10.055 --> 00:32:12.015
Relax. Mr. Spock.

616
00:32:12.098 --> 00:32:14.184
Which I know is
difficult for you.

617
00:32:14.309 --> 00:32:17.145
That's why the Lutrog.

618
00:32:19.397 --> 00:32:21.524
Careful with that.

619
00:32:21.649 --> 00:32:23.360
It seems clear by now

620
00:32:23.485 --> 00:32:24.736
that being confronted
with the truth

621
00:32:24.819 --> 00:32:26.112
is not enough to
break the spell.

622
00:32:26.112 --> 00:32:28.156
Which leaves us with
emotional response.

623
00:32:28.239 --> 00:32:29.449
But we have seen a
range of emotions

624
00:32:29.449 --> 00:32:31.451
and yet none dispel
the delusion.

625
00:32:34.079 --> 00:32:38.041
Anger. rage. it's one of the
most powerful emotions there is.

626
00:32:38.166 --> 00:32:42.128
Perhaps another equally
powerful emotion.

627
00:32:42.212 --> 00:32:43.672
Like what ?

628
00:32:43.797 --> 00:32:45.048
Love.

629
00:32:46.716 --> 00:32:48.301
Mr. Spock. I almost
forgot. the wedding planner

630
00:32:48.385 --> 00:32:50.178
asked you to weigh in on
the seating arrangement.

631
00:32:50.261 --> 00:32:52.889
Take a look at row
eight. if you don't mind.

632
00:32:52.972 --> 00:32:54.391
Uh. Captain ?

633
00:32:54.516 --> 00:32:56.685
How many guests are
invited to the wedding ?

634
00:32:56.810 --> 00:33:00.522
All the crew and. uh.
107 registered guests.

635
00:33:00.647 --> 00:33:02.190
Thanks.

636
00:33:03.233 --> 00:33:04.901
Computer. how many individuals

637
00:33:05.026 --> 00:33:06.403
are currently aboard
the Enterprise

638
00:33:06.486 --> 00:33:09.447
besides crew and
registered guests ?

639
00:33:10.281 --> 00:33:12.075
One.

640
00:33:12.200 --> 00:33:13.451
We have a wedding crasher.

641
00:33:13.576 --> 00:33:14.869
Hiding in plain sight.

642
00:33:14.953 --> 00:33:16.913
Computer. locate
that individual.

643
00:33:17.872 --> 00:33:19.749
The individual
fitting that description

644
00:33:19.833 --> 00:33:21.626
is in the Port Galley.

645
00:33:23.878 --> 00:33:25.964
Spock. where you going ?

646
00:33:26.089 --> 00:33:27.799
We're gonna do karaoke.

647
00:33:27.924 --> 00:33:31.094
Oh.
Mr. Korby. Mr. Spock.

648
00:33:31.219 --> 00:33:32.679
Shouldn't you be at
your bachelor party ?

649
00:33:32.762 --> 00:33:36.057
I'm working on a specialty
drink for the reception.

650
00:33:36.182 --> 00:33:37.892
How do we feel
about pomegranate ?

651
00:33:38.018 --> 00:33:39.936
I do not need a bacchanal.

652
00:33:40.020 --> 00:33:41.479
Then you should get
your beauty rest.

653
00:33:41.604 --> 00:33:43.440
I do not need to sleep.

654
00:33:43.523 --> 00:33:45.525
Count tribbles. then.

655
00:33:45.525 --> 00:33:47.152
You. You are the entity.

656
00:33:47.277 --> 00:33:48.778
Oh. Mr. Spock.

657
00:33:48.862 --> 00:33:51.239
Your Vulcan sense of
humor gets me every time.

658
00:33:51.364 --> 00:33:53.742
I'm your wedding
planner. remember ?

659
00:33:53.825 --> 00:33:56.661
You twirled into my
office. drunk on love.

660
00:33:56.786 --> 00:34:00.123
wishing for a wedding day full
of magic and unspeakable joy.

661
00:34:00.248 --> 00:34:01.916
A wish.

662
00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:03.335
That night. here
in the Port Galley.

663
00:34:03.418 --> 00:34:05.712
you were the
bartender then. too.

664
00:34:05.795 --> 00:34:08.298
I wished things could be
different with Christine.

665
00:34:08.381 --> 00:34:09.924
And you made it so.

666
00:34:10.050 --> 00:34:11.968
You're welcome.

667
00:34:12.052 --> 00:34:13.345
It does not matter.

668
00:34:13.470 --> 00:34:15.096
We are not going through
with the wedding.

669
00:34:15.180 --> 00:34:17.140
You have to fix this.

670
00:34:17.265 --> 00:34:19.601
You can't just control
people's minds.

671
00:34:19.726 --> 00:34:21.311
I can do anything I want.

672
00:34:21.394 --> 00:34:23.063
I am a wedding planner.

673
00:34:30.111 --> 00:34:34.115
And I do not like it when
people ruin my plans.

674
00:34:40.747 --> 00:34:44.084
Wakey wakey. Mr. Spock.
It's your big day.

675
00:34:44.167 --> 00:34:47.045
You cannot force me to
continue this charade.

676
00:34:47.170 --> 00:34:48.546
Can't I. though ? Do you know

677
00:34:48.672 --> 00:34:50.674
what would happen to
everyone if you made me mad ?

678
00:34:51.841 --> 00:34:53.718
I don't think I can
even imagine it.

679
00:34:58.223 --> 00:34:59.391
Well. look at that.

680
00:34:59.516 --> 00:35:01.601
My own little Vulcan terrarium.

681
00:35:01.726 --> 00:35:03.978
My friends will be so jealous.

682
00:35:05.855 --> 00:35:09.317
I do hope you'll
play along now. yes ?

683
00:35:14.197 --> 00:35:16.866
I can
hear the wedding bells.

684
00:35:39.597 --> 00:35:42.767
Ah ! Look at you. you look great.

685
00:35:42.892 --> 00:35:45.270
All weddings should
be on the beach

686
00:35:45.395 --> 00:35:47.063
and everyone should
be in shorts.

687
00:35:47.063 --> 00:35:48.356
Okay.

688
00:35:53.611 --> 00:35:55.321
I have been searching for you.

689
00:35:55.447 --> 00:35:57.574
He's made me the maid of honor.

690
00:35:57.574 --> 00:35:58.908
And he says if I
don't play along.

691
00:35:59.034 --> 00:36:01.077
he's gonna wish us
all to a cornfield.

692
00:36:01.202 --> 00:36:03.246
I do not understand the
significance of this wish.

693
00:36:03.371 --> 00:36:05.415
It's from a ... Doesn't matter.

694
00:36:05.540 --> 00:36:07.542
He's talking about wiping
us from all of existence.

695
00:36:07.625 --> 00:36:09.794
Yes. he made this
threat to me as well.

696
00:36:09.919 --> 00:36:11.921
You're gonna have to
go through with this.

697
00:36:11.921 --> 00:36:14.591
Just ... Maybe that's
the only way to end it.

698
00:36:14.591 --> 00:36:17.552
play his game.

699
00:36:17.635 --> 00:36:19.512
It's time. Spock.

700
00:36:19.596 --> 00:36:21.681
Let's get you married.

701
00:37:30.834 --> 00:37:33.211
Please be seated.

702
00:37:37.674 --> 00:37:39.384
What a delight

703
00:37:39.509 --> 00:37:43.513
to be gathered here today to
celebrate something so special.

704
00:37:43.596 --> 00:37:47.726
a force more powerful
than the fastest starship.

705
00:37:47.851 --> 00:37:50.020
Humans call it love.

706
00:37:50.020 --> 00:37:52.397
and I'm told love can conquer

707
00:37:52.522 --> 00:37:54.441
-all things.
-Christine ...

708
00:37:54.566 --> 00:37:56.401
Shh. Not yet.

709
00:38:01.031 --> 00:38:03.199
Do you both have your vows ?

710
00:38:03.283 --> 00:38:04.617
No.

711
00:38:04.743 --> 00:38:06.453
No !

712
00:38:06.536 --> 00:38:08.038
I object.

713
00:38:08.163 --> 00:38:10.373
-We're not there yet.
-Roger. what are you doing ?

714
00:38:10.373 --> 00:38:12.500
Christine. you
have to stop this.

715
00:38:12.584 --> 00:38:13.877
You stop.

716
00:38:14.002 --> 00:38:15.712
You can't just make
people feel things

717
00:38:15.712 --> 00:38:17.297
that they don't really feel !

718
00:38:17.380 --> 00:38:19.591
That's it.

719
00:38:21.760 --> 00:38:23.928
Aw ...

720
00:38:26.890 --> 00:38:29.976
Please. continue. Mr. Spock.

721
00:38:40.111 --> 00:38:42.572
The human poet Neruda wrote.

722
00:38:42.697 --> 00:38:45.950
"I crave your mouth. your voice.

723
00:38:46.076 --> 00:38:48.286
"your hair.

724
00:38:48.411 --> 00:38:49.913
"Silent and starving.

725
00:38:50.038 --> 00:38:52.415
"I prowl through the streets.

726
00:38:52.415 --> 00:38:54.793
"Bread does not nourish me.

727
00:38:54.918 --> 00:38:56.544
"dawn disrupts me.

728
00:38:56.628 --> 00:38:58.338
"all day

729
00:38:58.421 --> 00:39:01.633
I hunt for the liquid
measure of your steps."

730
00:39:03.093 --> 00:39:06.388
This is what it is like
to love you. Christine.

731
00:39:06.471 --> 00:39:09.599
And the person
worthy of your love.

732
00:39:09.724 --> 00:39:11.810
they must be courageous.

733
00:39:13.228 --> 00:39:15.271
They cannot be drowning.

734
00:39:15.397 --> 00:39:16.731
They cannot be unsure

735
00:39:16.815 --> 00:39:19.317
or at the mercy of their
own emotional storms.

736
00:39:20.485 --> 00:39:22.404
They must be a safe harbor.

737
00:39:23.697 --> 00:39:26.866
They must have the ability
to hold space for you.

738
00:39:27.826 --> 00:39:29.160
To see you.

739
00:39:29.285 --> 00:39:30.954
Just you.

740
00:39:32.163 --> 00:39:35.375
They must be able to
hear your unuttered call.

741
00:39:40.213 --> 00:39:42.590
They must be able to
give you everything.

742
00:39:45.844 --> 00:39:49.180
They must offer you the moon

743
00:39:49.305 --> 00:39:53.393
and the sun and the stars

744
00:39:53.518 --> 00:39:55.437
all at once.

745
00:39:59.399 --> 00:40:02.402
I did not know when it was
your mother's birthday.

746
00:40:03.194 --> 00:40:05.488
I didn't tell you.

747
00:40:05.488 --> 00:40:07.866
It's no one's fault.

748
00:40:11.995 --> 00:40:13.830
This is wrong. Spock.

749
00:40:17.667 --> 00:40:20.712
We're not supposed to
be getting married.

750
00:40:20.837 --> 00:40:22.088
No.

751
00:40:23.006 --> 00:40:24.716
We are not.

752
00:40:24.841 --> 00:40:26.760
Yes. you are.

753
00:40:26.843 --> 00:40:28.970
Roger ...

754
00:40:30.347 --> 00:40:31.348
Roger.

755
00:40:31.431 --> 00:40:32.891
Well. no. he's a dog.

756
00:40:33.016 --> 00:40:34.768
so ... No !

757
00:40:34.851 --> 00:40:36.436
No. no. no. no. no !

758
00:40:36.561 --> 00:40:37.896
That is it.

759
00:40:38.021 --> 00:40:39.564
Everybody dies.

760
00:40:40.357 --> 00:40:43.234
-And I'm starting with the dog.
-You keep away from him.

761
00:40:43.360 --> 00:40:45.403
Prepare for a
cavalcade of death.

762
00:40:45.528 --> 00:40:47.781
No one gets a wedding
cake slice tonight.

763
00:40:47.864 --> 00:40:50.033
You're going to
die. You'll be dead.

764
00:40:50.158 --> 00:40:52.118
And you with the crown.
what were you thinking ?

765
00:40:52.202 --> 00:40:53.703
Tried to outshine the bride ?

766
00:40:53.703 --> 00:40:56.790
And you blue faces. you
could see I was in blue.

767
00:40:56.915 --> 00:40:58.083
How dare you.

768
00:40:58.208 --> 00:41:00.043
Death to you. And
you at the back

769
00:41:00.126 --> 00:41:01.419
with no mouth.

770
00:41:01.544 --> 00:41:03.004
Yes. you.

771
00:41:03.088 --> 00:41:06.883
Actually. that's ... I like
that. You can. you can live.

772
00:41:07.008 --> 00:41:09.177
What is this ?

773
00:41:15.392 --> 00:41:16.893
Not now. Dad.

774
00:41:16.976 --> 00:41:18.353
Oh. you've
made enough of a mess.

775
00:41:18.436 --> 00:41:19.646
Please. let's not make a scene.

776
00:41:19.729 --> 00:41:22.565
Oh. my ...

777
00:41:22.565 --> 00:41:24.651
-Christine.
-Oh. Oh ...

778
00:41:24.776 --> 00:41:27.904
But they're not playing along.
They're not listening to me.

779
00:41:27.904 --> 00:41:29.906
And you
are not listening to me.

780
00:41:30.031 --> 00:41:32.784
Shall I show you once more
what the consequence is

781
00:41:32.909 --> 00:41:35.662
-for disobedience ?
-No.

782
00:41:36.871 --> 00:41:38.707
I'll be good. I promise.

783
00:41:38.790 --> 00:41:40.917
Wait. you're a child ?

784
00:41:41.001 --> 00:41:43.837
A very young one. Only
8.000 of your Earth years.

785
00:41:43.962 --> 00:41:45.630
8.020. Dad.

786
00:41:45.755 --> 00:41:48.299
-It's time to go.
-I don't want to go.

787
00:41:48.425 --> 00:41:50.802
Wait. before you leave ...

788
00:41:51.970 --> 00:41:54.180
 ...might I ask why ?

789
00:41:54.264 --> 00:41:55.265
Well ...

790
00:41:55.390 --> 00:41:57.100
Look at him.

791
00:41:57.100 --> 00:42:00.311
I spotted him digging in the
dirt on the old homeworld.

792
00:42:00.437 --> 00:42:04.190
He's just so handsome
and smart and perfect.

793
00:42:04.315 --> 00:42:06.359
It's just annoying.

794
00:42:06.443 --> 00:42:08.278
Yes. that does
make perfect sense.

795
00:42:08.278 --> 00:42:10.280
-Oy.
-Now ...

796
00:42:10.363 --> 00:42:12.449
-free the rest of them.
-Okay.

797
00:42:21.291 --> 00:42:23.001
Tallyho.

798
00:42:23.126 --> 00:42:25.545
You've all been lots of fun.

799
00:42:47.650 --> 00:42:50.403
Uh ...

800
00:42:50.487 --> 00:42:51.738
Okay. everybody. all
right. all right.

801
00:42:51.821 --> 00:42:53.281
all right. all right.
okay. all right.

802
00:42:53.365 --> 00:42:56.951
That was. uh. that-that-that ...
that was strange.

803
00:42:57.035 --> 00:42:59.120
A shared delusion
about a wedding

804
00:42:59.204 --> 00:43:01.081
is a new one. isn't
it ?

805
00:43:01.164 --> 00:43:04.084
Okay ... Uh. Federation Day.

806
00:43:04.209 --> 00:43:06.544
2161. the. uh. founding species

807
00:43:06.670 --> 00:43:10.840
came together to create.
uh. the Federation.

808
00:43:10.924 --> 00:43:12.342
Um. largely in response

809
00:43:12.425 --> 00:43:15.053
to our interactions with
other foreign species.

810
00:43:15.178 --> 00:43:16.680
Some of them very awkward.

811
00:43:16.805 --> 00:43:19.432
Uh. so it's only fitting

812
00:43:19.557 --> 00:43:22.352
that-that our-our
centennial be marked

813
00:43:22.352 --> 00:43:25.563
by a-a-a similar awkward.

814
00:43:25.689 --> 00:43:28.149
uh. interaction.

815
00:43:31.695 --> 00:43:33.738
And the bar is open.

816
00:43:45.625 --> 00:43:47.210
Those
look incredible.

817
00:43:47.293 --> 00:43:50.255
I'll make you
one. but it's Alanni Rye.

818
00:43:50.380 --> 00:43:53.383
It will burn a hole
through your esophagus

819
00:43:53.466 --> 00:43:56.219
and whatever is
below your esophagus.

820
00:43:56.344 --> 00:43:58.138
And maybe the floor.

821
00:43:58.263 --> 00:43:59.389
Two pints of Guinness. please.

822
00:43:59.389 --> 00:44:01.766
Probably a safer bet.

823
00:44:01.891 --> 00:44:03.685
Are you the doctor
from the Enterprise ?

824
00:44:03.768 --> 00:44:06.604
Joseph M'Benga.

825
00:44:16.489 --> 00:44:17.615
Mm.

826
00:44:19.868 --> 00:44:22.037
You know. I kind of
miss the flower crown.

827
00:44:22.120 --> 00:44:23.329
-Oh. yeah ?
-Mm.

828
00:44:23.413 --> 00:44:25.248
I kind of miss the
big green veil thing

829
00:44:25.248 --> 00:44:26.750
you had going on.

830
00:44:26.833 --> 00:44:28.543
Well. I can tell you it
is not every girl's dream

831
00:44:28.626 --> 00:44:31.796
to have a cosmic trickster
play dress-up dolls

832
00:44:31.921 --> 00:44:33.631
with her emotions

833
00:44:33.757 --> 00:44:36.259
and make her marry
the wrong man.

834
00:44:36.259 --> 00:44:40.221
-The last 48 hours have been ...
-Roger.

835
00:44:41.097 --> 00:44:42.599
I know.

836
00:44:44.642 --> 00:44:46.019
Me. too.

837
00:44:47.103 --> 00:44:50.398
Now. let's go dance and
never talk about this

838
00:44:50.482 --> 00:44:51.983
ever.

839
00:44:52.108 --> 00:44:53.401
Deal.

840
00:45:02.077 --> 00:45:03.953
You thinking what I'm thinking ?

841
00:45:04.079 --> 00:45:06.122
Mm-hmm. If we
play our cards right.

842
00:45:06.247 --> 00:45:08.291
Oh. we were just
saying that an artist

843
00:45:08.291 --> 00:45:09.584
with such prodigious skills

844
00:45:09.668 --> 00:45:11.127
shouldn't be confined
to a starbase.

845
00:45:11.127 --> 00:45:15.632
If you're offering me
a job on a starship.

846
00:45:15.715 --> 00:45:17.550
my answer is yes.

847
00:45:18.843 --> 00:45:20.053
Thank you.

848
00:45:20.136 --> 00:45:22.222
-Pleasure meeting you.
-Thank you.

849
00:45:22.347 --> 00:45:24.349
I just had a very
interesting conversation

850
00:45:24.474 --> 00:45:26.476
with the Chancellor of
Starfleet's Public Relations.

851
00:45:26.476 --> 00:45:27.852
-Yeah ?
-They may commission

852
00:45:27.977 --> 00:45:30.063
a feature-length
documentary of Starfleet.

853
00:45:30.188 --> 00:45:33.817
Well. the Chancellor likes me.
so I'll put in a good word.

854
00:45:33.900 --> 00:45:37.696
You know. anything
to annoy Erica.

855
00:45:37.821 --> 00:45:40.073
-Shall we annoy Erica ?
-To annoying Erica.

856
00:45:40.156 --> 00:45:41.366
-To annoying Erica.
-Mm-hmm.

857
00:46:03.179 --> 00:46:05.932
That was a beautiful speech.

858
00:46:07.225 --> 00:46:09.144
Yes. I suppose so.

859
00:46:10.729 --> 00:46:13.398
Love comes in all
forms. Mr. Spock.

860
00:46:13.523 --> 00:46:16.026
and you gave her yours.

861
00:46:19.487 --> 00:46:20.864
And I have no regrets.

862
00:46:23.324 --> 00:46:25.744
Still. it is a waste.

863
00:46:25.869 --> 00:46:27.203
What is ?

864
00:46:27.287 --> 00:46:28.788
Well. you spent all this
time learning to dance.

865
00:46:28.872 --> 00:46:29.789
and now you're just

866
00:46:29.914 --> 00:46:31.458
sitting on it.

867
00:46:33.043 --> 00:46:34.711
After all. your
shoulder placement

868
00:46:34.794 --> 00:46:37.297
has been measured
precisely. has it not ?

869
00:46:38.089 --> 00:46:39.966
If I'm not mistaken.

870
00:46:40.050 --> 00:46:42.052
I am not supposed
to measure them.

871
00:46:42.177 --> 00:46:43.762
I am supposed to let them flow.

872
00:46:45.055 --> 00:46:47.057
Lieutenant ...

873
00:46:47.057 --> 00:46:48.433
are you asking me to dance ?

874
00:46:48.558 --> 00:46:50.852
♪ Jitterbug ♪

875
00:46:51.936 --> 00:46:53.646
♪ Jitterbug ♪

876
00:46:53.772 --> 00:46:54.814
It's all you. It's all you.

877
00:46:54.898 --> 00:46:56.274
♪ Jitterbug ♪

878
00:46:57.442 --> 00:46:59.402
♪ Jitterbug ♪

879
00:47:00.403 --> 00:47:03.239
♪ You put the boom
boom into my heart ♪

880
00:47:03.239 --> 00:47:06.117
♪ You send my soul sky high
when your loving starts ♪

881
00:47:06.242 --> 00:47:09.245
-♪ Jitterbug into my brain ♪
-♪ Yeah. yeah ♪

882
00:47:09.245 --> 00:47:12.832
♪ Goes a bang-bang-bang
till my feet do the same ♪

883
00:47:12.916 --> 00:47:15.919
♪ But something's bugging
me. something ain't right ♪

884
00:47:15.919 --> 00:47:18.922
♪ My best friend told me
what you did last night ♪

885
00:47:19.005 --> 00:47:21.299
♪ Left me sleeping in my bed ♪

886
00:47:21.424 --> 00:47:23.009
♪ I was dreaming ♪

887
00:47:23.093 --> 00:47:25.428
♪ But I should've been
with you instead ♪

888
00:47:25.428 --> 00:47:27.430
♪ Wake me up before you go-go ♪

889
00:47:27.430 --> 00:47:30.975
♪ Don't leave me hanging
on like a yo-yo ♪

890
00:47:31.101 --> 00:47:33.812
♪ Wake me up before you go-go ♪

891
00:47:33.937 --> 00:47:36.815
♪ I don't want to miss it
when you hit that high ♪

892
00:47:36.940 --> 00:47:39.693
♪ Wake me up before you go-go ♪

893
00:47:39.818 --> 00:47:42.821
♪ 'Cause I'm not
planning on going solo ♪

894
00:47:42.946 --> 00:47:46.366
♪ Wake me up before you go-go ♪

895
00:47:46.491 --> 00:47:49.786
♪ Take me dancing tonight ♪

896
00:47:52.539 --> 00:47:55.291
♪ I want to hit that high. ♪
